>
>  How does this work? I thought that altar alignment determined what
>happens to water- not character alignment.
>
>  Have I missed a means of blessing/cursing water?

You are right; the altar's alignment does indeed determine what type of
water is created.  I wasn't specific enough in the above statements, but
I was talking about alignment, not creating various types of water.

What I meant was: 
Become lawful so you can create lawful altars from other types.  Then, make
as much holy water as you want.

Become chaotic so you can create chaotic altars from other types.  Then, make
as much unholy water as you want.

Sorry about the confusion.

ADDITIONAL SPOILERS

To create a lawful altar from a neutral or chaotic altar, become lawful and
sacrifice fresh corpses until it becomes lawful.  You will loose luck each
time you fail, and you will gain luck when you are successful.

The same method can be used to create chaotic altars with the same luck
modifications.
